\caption{BCS-controlled FewRel accuracy. The confusability gap between low-BCS and high-BCS batches widens from 9.1\,pp at 16 relations to 31.2\,pp at 80 relations ($3.4\times$ amplification).}
\label{fig:bcs_scaling}
\end{figure}

At the 16-relation scale, switching from low-BCS to high-BCS batches reduces accuracy by 9.1 percentage points.

We now decompose extraction errors into an error taxonomy to distinguish the mechanisms behind performance loss. Figure~\ref{fig:error_taxonomy} illustrates the taxonomy; Table~\ref{tab:error_taxonomy} quantifies how each error type scales with BCS.

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{../../figures/paper/fig_error_taxonomy.pdf}
\caption{Error taxonomy decomposition. IntraSub (intra-batch substitution) scales monotonically with BCS, while missed-entity rates remain flat, confirming that confusability drives type confusion independently of detection failure.}
\label{fig:error_taxonomy}
\end{figure}

